WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.140
Here's something interesting.

00:00:01.140 --> 00:00:06.729
Last week I told you about Republican governor
from Ohio, Mike DeWine, who essentially abandoned

00:00:06.729 --> 00:00:09.190
Donald Trump when it comes to dealing with
Corona virus.

00:00:09.190 --> 00:00:13.629
Mike DeWine took her own virus seriously from
quite early on.

00:00:13.629 --> 00:00:16.250
One of one of the earlier governors to really
take action.

00:00:16.250 --> 00:00:21.720
And he has seen his approval skyrocket thanks
to not following the Trump doctrine and following

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:24.970
these sort of sensible governor doctrine on
coronavirus.

00:00:24.970 --> 00:00:29.500
We've now learned that Republican Congressman
Peter King from New York, who I am no big

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:36.150
fan of, is going to be ignoring the Republican
Party and voting for a Democratic coronavirus

00:00:36.150 --> 00:00:39.120
relief package that's expected to be voted
on later today.

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:42.900
If it may already have been voted on by the
time you listened to today's show.

00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:48.590
Now, I have mixed feelings about this in the
sense that it is once again, it's a Republican

00:00:48.590 --> 00:00:53.120
who's personally affected by something and
now is behaving rationally and doing the right

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:54.750
empathetic thing.

00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:58.870
I wish it didn't take that to get them to
behave appropriately.

00:00:58.870 --> 00:01:03.100
And what I mean by that is Peter King is a
New York congressman.

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:06.190
He represents one of the hardest hit areas
by the virus.

00:01:06.190 --> 00:01:08.580
It's New York's second congressional district.

00:01:08.580 --> 00:01:10.350
This is the south shore of Long Island.

00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:15.860
So it's not the absolute epicenter of New
York City's five boroughs, but it's as close

00:01:15.860 --> 00:01:16.860
as you can be.

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:20.980
It's it's just, you know, the New York City
metro area without actually being there.

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:24.570
And that's why he's going to vote in favor
of this package.

00:01:24.570 --> 00:01:28.870
Republicans have been talking more and more
about what if we maybe limit relief to blue

00:01:28.870 --> 00:01:29.870
states.

00:01:29.870 --> 00:01:32.560
They've been hesitant to do more relief and
a second stimulus.

00:01:32.560 --> 00:01:34.300
But Peter King can't get away with that.

00:01:34.300 --> 00:01:36.820
His district has been absolutely crushed.

00:01:36.820 --> 00:01:41.150
So there are some who are framing this as
hero.

00:01:41.150 --> 00:01:44.660
Peter King abandons his party and does the
right thing.

00:01:44.660 --> 00:01:50.030
Well, it's more like Peter King abandons his
party on this one, bill, because it would

00:01:50.030 --> 00:01:54.990
be political suicide for him personally not
to, since he represents one of the hardest

00:01:54.990 --> 00:01:57.570
hit congressional districts in the country.

00:01:57.570 --> 00:02:03.310
If it were the Boston area or Seattle that
needed this particular type of bill and not

00:02:03.310 --> 00:02:06.131
his district, my guess is he would not be
voting for it.

00:02:06.131 --> 00:02:09.030
He would simply stick it out with Republicans.

00:02:09.030 --> 00:02:14.240
Peter King is normally no friend of the left
or of the Democratic Party.

00:02:14.240 --> 00:02:16.390
And this is one.

00:02:16.390 --> 00:02:21.670
It's a horrible realization that we have to
have what it takes for some of these people

00:02:21.670 --> 00:02:26.900
to do something, to do the right thing is
to be personally affected.

00:02:26.900 --> 00:02:29.230
He needs to be reelected in November.

00:02:29.230 --> 00:02:31.620
So that's why he has to do this.

00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:34.920
Now, as far as the bill goes, there are actually
some really interesting things in it.

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:38.700
This is called the Heroes Act, 3 trillion
in total.

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:47.770
It stands for the Health and Economic Recovery
Omnibus Emergency Solutions Act Heroes Act.

00:02:47.770 --> 00:02:53.310
It would pay a company's payroll costs up
to one hundred thousand dollars per employee

00:02:53.310 --> 00:02:55.420
who has been laid off or furloughed.

00:02:55.420 --> 00:03:01.121
If the business can demonstrate that their
revenue has dropped at least 20 percent, it

00:03:01.121 --> 00:03:04.780
would add eight hundred and fifty billion
in assistance to state and local governments.

00:03:04.780 --> 00:03:10.550
Two hundred billion in hazard pay for frontline
health care workers and other non-essential

00:03:10.550 --> 00:03:11.550
workers.

00:03:11.550 --> 00:03:15.430
It would do another round of twelve hundred
dollar checks to most Americans.

00:03:15.430 --> 00:03:20.500
It would raise the payment per child from
five hundred dollars also to twelve hundred

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:25.080
dollars, but it would be capped total at six
thousand dollars per family.

00:03:25.080 --> 00:03:29.070
It would extend the supplemental, or I guess
they're calling it enhanced unemployment from

00:03:29.070 --> 00:03:33.750
the federal government through January 30,
first of next year.

00:03:33.750 --> 00:03:37.170
And one of the most interesting components
that's buried in there, which I don't actually

00:03:37.170 --> 00:03:41.901
think will pass if the bill does pass, is
that it will eliminate the ten thousand dollar

00:03:41.901 --> 00:03:47.210
cap on what's called salt state and local
taxes for 2020 and 2021.

00:03:47.210 --> 00:03:51.320
This is super interesting because one of the
ways that the Trump Republican tax reform

00:03:51.320 --> 00:03:59.970
of 2017 hurt those in states like mostly blue
blue states with higher state income taxes

00:03:59.970 --> 00:04:04.560
is they limited the state and local tax deduction
to $10000.

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:09.200
So if you live in a very high tax state or
just a blue state with a reasonable amount

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:14.709
of tax, you are limited in what amount of
tax you can write off on your federal return

00:04:14.709 --> 00:04:16.209
to $10000 total.

00:04:16.209 --> 00:04:22.810
This goes directly at blue states and it tends
to have no effect in some of these red states

00:04:22.810 --> 00:04:24.439
that have no state income tax.

00:04:24.439 --> 00:04:29.520
So it would repeal that for 2020 and 2021,
which is very, very interesting.

00:04:29.520 --> 00:04:36.550
Although analysts agree it is very unlikely
that that suspension of the $10000 salt cap

00:04:36.550 --> 00:04:41.860
would actually make it into a final bill that
passes Senate and House conference.

00:04:41.860 --> 00:04:44.319
But in the meantime, we will see how the House
votes.

00:04:44.319 --> 00:04:45.990
Peter King apparently will be voting with
Democrats.

00:04:45.990 --> 00:04:46.650
And we will follow it.

